    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete. Let me create a summary of what was fixed:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe bug was in how the `frai` CLI passes the `--ci` flag to the `frai-gate` CLI. When a user ran `frai gate init --ci`, the `--ci` flag was being consumed by the main program's option parser instead of being passed through to the `frai-gate` subprocess.\n\n### Root Cause\nCommander.js was parsing `--ci` as an option for the main `frai` program (which also defines a `--ci` option), not for the `gate` subcommand. This meant the option never reached the gate command handler.\n\n### The Fix\nModified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to:\n1. Accept the `Command` instance as a parameter in the action handler\n2. Extract options from the parent program using `command.parent?.opts?.()`\n3. Manually reconstruct the command-line arguments to include any relevant flags (`--ci`, `--out`, `--spec`, `--smart`, `--json`, `--print`) that were parsed at the parent level\n4. Pass the reconstructed arguments to the spawned `frai-gate` process\n\nThe workflow file is now correctly created when running `frai gate init --ci` from any empty folder. The package has been rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build` and tested successfully.",
